# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to Cloud Build (runbook §3.3).
# Without this file gcloud skips everything .gitignore lists, which includes data/, so the
# Dockerfile's copy of the corpus and embedding cache fails. An allow-list like .dockerignore:
# nothing else leaves the machine, so .env, serviceAccountKey.json, .claude/ and eval/ stay out.
# Patterns follow .gitignore rules, not Docker's: a file under an excluded directory cannot be
# let back in, so each directory on the way to a data file is re-included and then emptied.
# Check with `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload .`.
/*
!/.gcloudignore
!/.dockerignore
!/Dockerfile
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/tsconfig.json
!/src/
!/release/
/release/*
!/release/artifacts.sha256

# The two approved data files (release plan S1), checked against release/artifacts.sha256.
!/data/
/data/*
!/data/corpus/
/data/corpus/*
!/data/corpus/corpus.json
!/data/embeddings/
/data/embeddings/*
!/data/embeddings/cache.json
